{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794352090000-engineer-cc2-fix-r3.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md; git diff --stat; git diff -- src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-10 23:17:50 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 06:17:50 +07\n\n# cc2 fix round r3 — the admission-identity residue (1 carried P0, 1 new P0, test gaps)\n\nWorktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2`, branch `cc2-transform-session-c1` @ `2d170926`, left dirty, NOTHING committed (orchestrator commits after reviewer confirmation). Bounds respected: only four of the six permitted files changed (`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc`, `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`); `vm/macro.cljc`, `vm/semantic/*`, `yang/clojure.cljc`, `core/prelude.cljc`, `vm/linker/dht.cljc`, `vm.cljc` untouched — no fix required them. Origins never minted; canonical bytes unchanged; legacy paths byte-identical; fail-closed everywhere. The pre-existing untracked `CC2-REVIEW-R2.md` was left untouched.\n\nNOTE (placement): this session's sandbox permits writes only under the cc2 worktree, so this file was written to the worktree's own `collab/yang-clojure/` mirror of the deliverable path `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794352090000-engineer-cc2-fix-r3.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md` (write probe to the external path: Operation not permitted). The orchestrator can move it verbatim; no prior findings file was touched either way.\n\n## Per-finding disposition\n\n### 1. F2 P0 — counter equality is not admission identity (was publish.cljc:582)\n\nFixed. The expander's retained tables already key by full origin (`[[:source medium batch-token member-index] final-root]`, `yin.vm.macro/call-site-table`); no parallel structure was invented — that key is now resolved exactly, and the missing link (which indexed program that origin belongs to) is carried as an explicit mapping recorded where the index and the expander actually agree.\n\n- [src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1217): `call-site-admissions` exposes the session's `{indexed-program-metadata-entity full-admission-origin}` mapping; [record-call-site-admissions:1247](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1247), wired into `eval-program` (line 1749) at the one point both sides commit the same staged packet — the round the expander retained a new `[origin root]` table entry is the round the indexer committed that program — pairs the entry's full origin with the newly indexed program of the same root read back from the published index. Only a uniquely identifiable program is paired; ambiguity (e.g. an earlier unclaimed admission of the same root) leaves the program unmapped. No counter is read or compared anywhere in the pairing. Session state carries the mapping from `make-session` (line 788); `link-context` forwards it (line 1382).\n- [src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc:816): one forwarding line, `:call-site-admissions` into `publish-name!` opts (which already passes opts whole to `module-from-index`; `dht.cljc` untouched).\n- [src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:560): `retained-call-site-rows` now takes `admissions`, looks up the program's full origin by its metadata entity `(:m program)`, and resolves `(get tables [origin root])` exactly. The old root + `(:t program)` == batch-token filter is deleted. Mapping absent, origin malformed, or the named entry absent → nil → recovery refused (claim-free publication, unchanged policy). A matched table must still prove itself (five-coordinate rows, ruled origins, version 1, unique ownership, exact coverage). `module-from-index` (line 773, 823) accepts `:call-site-admissions` beside `:call-site-tables`.\n- Drift behaviour: with an explicit mapping, a program whose batch and `t` have drifted still resolves its own table exactly (test b2); in the astra collision shape — second admission at batch+1, indexed program carrying batch `b`, no mapping supplied for it — nothing is borrowed from the batch-`b` table and publication is claim-free (test b).\n\n### 2. NEW P0 — uncovered applications silently claimed as wrappers (was publish.cljc:659)\n\nFixed. Wrapperhood is no longer inferred from non-coverage.\n\n- [publish.cljc:620](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:620): `sequenced-wrapper-paths` computes the assembled-tree path of each `sequenced` wrapper; `module-from-index` emits them on the spec as the explicit `:call-site-wrappers` occurrence set (`[final-root path]` pairs, line 871), and assembly itself verifies shifted rows + wrappers account for the final tree exactly before any claim is emitted.\n- [publish.cljc:630](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:630): `recovered-call-site-claim` now takes the wrapper set (wired at line 291). Recovered rows ∪ explicit wrappers must cover the tree EXACTLY: any other uncovered application refuses as `{:missing [...] :extra [...]}` → `publish-module!` refuses `:yin.link.publish/incomplete-call-site-coverage`, naming the unmapped occurrence; a wrapper naming a covered or non-existent place refuses as `:extra`. Only the explicit wrappers are claimed under the publication admission.\n- `[]`/nil `:call-site-rows` (and tables with no C1 rows) return nil from the claim step: a claim-free publication, never a full claim (test d); `[]`/nil/`{}` `:call-site-tables` at the index boundary likewise publish claim-free (test d2).\n\n### 3. F5 — test gaps (test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc)\n\nFixed. New `module-from-index-c1-r3-test` (line 1771) plus updated session specs to pass the explicit mapping (lines 1455, 1704, 1717, 1727):\n\n- (a) line 1789: sole foreign table, same root and same batch number, different medium/member → claim-free, not accepted.\n- (b) line 1798: drift collision (second admission at batch+1, no explicit mapping for the drifted program) → claim-free, not borrowed; (b2) line 1812: explicit mapping whose batch ≠ the program's `t` resolves exactly to the mapped admission's table (distinct row origin asserted).\n- (c) line 1825: one retained row deleted from a valid spec → publication REFUSED, reason `:yin.link.publish/incomplete-call-site-coverage`, and `:missing` names the deleted `[root path]` occurrence; wrapper-set tampering (`pop`) likewise refused (line 1835).\n- (d) line 1844: `:call-site-rows` `[]` and nil → publishes with no `:call-sites`; (d2) `:call-site-tables` `[]`/nil/`{}` → claim-free spec.\n\nRed-first evidence: after the test edits (and only the repl/query threading needed to compile), the suite ran **29 tests, 334 assertions, 9 failures, 0 errors** — every failure inside the new r3 cases (foreign table borrowed, drift borrowed, deleted row silently reassigned and published with a side table, `[]`/nil fully claimed, no `:call-site-wrappers` emitted). After the publish fix: 0 failures, same 334 assertions.\n\n## Verification (all foreground, nothing backgrounded)\n\n| Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` (pre-fix, r3 tests) | 29 tests, 334 assertions, **9 failures**, 0 errors (authentic reproduction) |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` (final) | **29 tests, 334 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.linker.publish-test -n yang.safepoint-test -n yin.repl.query-test` | **48 tests, 453 assertions, 0 failures** |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.index-test` (repl threading regression) | **73 tests, 510 assertions, 0 failures** |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.linker.dht-test -n yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test -n yin.repl.dht-test` (publish-name path) | **69 tests, 827 assertions, 0 failures** |\n| `clj -M:kondo --lint` (4 changed files) | **0 errors, 0 warnings** |\n\n## Notes / unverified\n\n- Fail-closed by design: a claimed admission the session round cannot pair uniquely (earlier unclaimed admission of the same root, index read-back unavailable, session rebuilt/`(reset)` — the mapping is session state and does not survive a rebuild while the carried-over index does) publishes claim-free rather than borrowing. This matches the stated refusal policy.\n- An assembly whose recovered programs contain no applications at all (rows `[]`, wrappers only) now publishes claim-free instead of claiming the wrappers alone — the empty-table rule of item 2 applied uniformly; no wrong claim is possible.\n- The kit contract test was not run (orchestrator runs it separately, per prior rounds).\n src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc               |  74 +++++++++++-\n src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc         |   1 +\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc  | 211 ++++++++++++++++++++++-------------\n test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | 115 ++++++++++++++++++-\n 4 files changed, 318 insertions(+), 83 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\nindex 66affee2..cd962463 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@\n             [yin.vm.module :as module]\n             [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n             [yin.vm.values :as values]\n+            [dao.space.index :as space-index]\n             [dao.stream.observer :as observer]))\n \n \n@@ -784,6 +785,7 @@\n      :program-identity (:identity program-in)\n      :observer (:observer program-in)\n      :expander (make-expander (:identity program-in) (:stream program-out))\n+     :call-site-admissions {}\n      :row-stream (:stream program-out)\n      :row-observer (:observer program-out)\n      :indexer (index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))\n@@ -1212,6 +1214,68 @@\n   (:call-site-tables (:expander state)))\n \n \n+(defn call-site-admissions\n+  \"The explicit indexed-program -> full-admission-origin mapping the\n+   session records at the point where the expander and the code indexer\n+   agree: the round in which the expander staged a program (retaining\n+   its table under `[admission-origin final-root]`) is the round in\n+   which the indexer committed that same program, so the newly indexed\n+   program's metadata entity is paired with that entry's full origin\n+   (`yin.vm.linker.publish/module-from-index`'\n+   `:call-site-admissions` option). No counter is compared: a program\n+   the round cannot pair uniquely is left unmapped, and recovery for\n+   it is refused. Empty before any claimed, indexed expansion.\"\n+  [state]\n+  (:call-site-admissions state))\n+\n+\n+(defn- indexed-program-roots\n+  \"The `[metadata-entity root]` of every program the indexer has\n+   published, or nil when the published index cannot be read.\"\n+  [indexer]\n+  (try\n+    (when (:manifest-address indexer)\n+      (into []\n+            (comp (filter (fn [[_e a _v _t _m]] (= :yin.repl/root a)))\n+                  (map (fn [[e _a v _t _m]] [e v])))\n+            (space-index/read-datoms (:content-store indexer)\n+                                     (:manifest-address indexer))))\n+    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _\n+      nil)))\n+\n+\n+(defn- record-call-site-admissions\n+  \"Pair each table entry the expander retained since `tables-before`\n+   with the indexed program this round committed under the same root,\n+   recording `{metadata-entity full-admission-origin}` on `state`.\n+   Only a uniquely identifiable program is paired; anything else is\n+   left unmapped (fail-closed), never inferred from counters.\"\n+  [tables-before state]\n+  (let [new-entries (into {}\n+                          (remove (fn [[k _]]\n+                                    (contains? tables-before k)))\n+                          (or (call-site-tables state) {}))]\n+    (if (empty? new-entries)\n+      state\n+      (if-let [programs (indexed-program-roots (:indexer state))]\n+        (reduce (fn [st [[origin root] _rows]]\n+                  (let [candidates\n+                        (filter (fn [[m r]]\n+                                  (and (= r root)\n+                                       (not (contains?\n+                                              (:call-site-admissions st)\n+                                              m))))\n+                                programs)]\n+                    (if (= 1 (count candidates))\n+                      (assoc-in st [:call-site-admissions\n+                                    (ffirst candidates)]\n+                                origin)\n+                      st)))\n+                (update state :call-site-admissions #(or % {}))\n+                new-entries)\n+        state))))\n+\n+\n (defn- run-expander-stage\n   \"Drive the expander over `program-in` and drain its summary.  It expands\n    each observed batch and appends the tree packet to `program-out`; a\n@@ -1315,6 +1379,7 @@\n    :primitives (:primitives vm)\n    :modules (:modules vm)\n    :call-site-tables (call-site-tables state)\n+   :call-site-admissions (call-site-admissions state)\n    :round (:round state)})\n \n \n@@ -1661,6 +1726,7 @@ Hint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n   (if (:ingress-loss? state)\n     [state (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n     (let [state' (update (inject-last-value state) :round inc)\n+          tables-before (call-site-tables state')\n           batch (encoder/program-batch program)\n           append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n       (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n@@ -1676,8 +1742,12 @@ Hint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n             failed\n             (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded\n                   indexed (cond-> expanded\n-                            (pos? forwarded) (-> run-index-stage\n-                                                 run-ast-index-stage))]\n+                            (pos? forwarded)\n+                            (-> run-index-stage\n+                                run-ast-index-stage\n+                                ((fn [s]\n+                                   (record-call-site-admissions\n+                                     tables-before s)))))]\n               (with-index-notice\n                 (cond\n                   (> (ingress-gaps indexed) (ingress-gaps state'))\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc\nindex e4540abf..7c78d9ed 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc\n@@ -813,6 +813,7 @@\n                                    :primitives (:primitives ctx)\n                                    :modules linked\n                                    :call-site-tables (:call-site-tables ctx)\n+                                   :call-site-admissions (:call-site-admissions ctx)\n                                    :host-modules hosts})\n                     indexer' (if (seq (:envelopes res))\n                                (repl.index/commit-names indexer (:envelopes res)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
