{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '420,487p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1900,1945p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | sed -n '620,709p'\"","aggregated_output":"   420\t  \"Publish the covered indexes over every committed transaction, using\n   421\t   the retained frontier when valid, drain the intake, and read the\n   422\t   manifest back from it.  Only a publication whose manifest the store\n   423\t   answers becomes the reported one, covering `:published` transactions;\n   424\t   in durable mode the HEAD pointer moves — `after-publish` — only after\n   425\t   that read-back, so a HEAD never names a manifest the store cannot\n   426\t   answer, and a HEAD that cannot be written leaves the round reported\n   427\t   unpublished.\"\n   428\t  [ix round]\n   429\t  (try\n   430\t    (let [{:keys [pool]} (:publication ix)\n   431\t          {:keys [manifest-address manifest cursor]} (enqueue-publication ix)\n   432\t          [n defect] (materialize (:content-store ix) pool)]\n   433\t      (if defect\n   434\t        (assoc ix :failure {:round round :stage :materialize :outcome defect})\n   435\t        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n   436\t            (when-some [write-head! (:after-publish ix)]\n   437\t              (write-head! manifest-address))\n   438\t            (cond-> (assoc ix\n   439\t                           :manifest-address manifest-address\n   440\t                           :published (:transactions ix)\n   441\t                           :published-payloads n\n   442\t                           :materialization {:cursor cursor\n   443\t                                             :transactions (:transactions ix)\n   444\t                                             :manifest-address manifest-address\n   445\t                                             :manifest manifest\n   446\t                                             :max-t (dec (transactor/watermark (:allocator ix)))})\n   447\t              (= :publish (:stage (:failure ix))) (assoc :failure nil)))))\n   448\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   449\t      (assoc ix\n   450\t             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n   451\t\n   452\t\n   453\t(defn- consume\n   454\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   455\t   to `f` with the indexer; a gap marks the indexer lost, after which no\n   456\t   packet reaches `f`.\"\n   457\t  [indexer f]\n   458\t  (loop [ix indexer]\n   459\t    (let [{:keys [status batch] observer' :observer}\n   460\t          (observer/observe-next (:observer ix))\n   461\t          ix (assoc ix :observer observer')]\n   462\t      (case status\n   463\t        :ok (recur (if (:lost? ix) ix (f ix batch)))\n   464\t        :gap (recur (assoc ix :lost? true))\n   465\t        ix))))\n   466\t\n   467\t\n   468\t(defn step\n   469\t  \"The round's index step: observe every packet `program-out` still holds\n   470\t   for this observer, commit each through the round's publication, publish\n   471\t   when any was committed, then drop the publication's intake, pool and\n   472\t   temporary trees. Only the detached allocator and verified covered\n   473\t   frontier continue into the next round. A gap is counted on the observer's\n   474\t   `:ingress-gaps`, and marks the indexer lost: the missing packet and\n   475\t   every later one are never called indexed.\"\n   476\t  [indexer round]\n   477\t  (let [ix (consume indexer\n   478\t                    (fn [ix packet]\n   479\t                      (first (commit (open-publication ix) packet round))))\n   480\t        committed? (> (:transactions ix) (:transactions indexer))\n   481\t        ;; this round's rows and any an earlier round could not write,\n   482\t        ;; before any publication: no announcement names a missing row\n   483\t        ix (if committed? (write-rows ix round) ix)]\n   484\t    (dissoc (if (and committed? (empty? (:unwritten ix)))\n   485\t              (publish ix round)\n   486\t              ix)\n   487\t            :publication)))\n  1900\t         (if tree\n  1901\t           (str \"\\n\\nExpanded rows:\\n\" (format-value tree))\n  1902\t           (str \"\\n\\nExpansion error:\\n\" (format-value error)))\n  1903\t         (when (seq frontend-metadata)\n  1904\t           (str \"\\n\\nCall sites:\\n\" (format-value frontend-metadata)))\n  1905\t         \"\\n\\nEvents:\\n\" (format-value (second log)))))\n  1906\t\n  1907\t\n  1908\t(defn- rebuild-session\n  1909\t  \"Replace the VM, the expander, and their media, attachments, and\n  1910\t   observers.  The value history is cleared with them: a closure in `*1`\n  1911\t   names a code segment the old VM held, which the new one does not.  The\n  1912\t   new expander holds only the standard forms.  A require still pending\n  1913\t   on the old VM is dropped with it: its link pair is the session's, and\n  1914\t   the new session answers from its own.\n  1915\t\n  1916\t   Over a durable store the code index is not the session's to drop: the\n  1917\t   new indexer continues the old one's log, entity allocation, and\n  1918\t   published manifest (`yin.repl.index/carry-over`), so a rebuild never\n  1919\t   resets `t`.  Over the memory store it starts empty, as it always has.\"\n  1920\t  [state vm-type]\n  1921\t  (merge state\n  1922\t         (cond-> (make-session vm-type (:output-stream state)\n  1923\t                               (merge (selected-primitives (:frontends state)\n  1924\t                                                           (:lang state))\n  1925\t                                      (:extra-primitives state))\n  1926\t                               (:shell-token state)\n  1927\t                               (:index-store state)\n  1928\t                               (:link-source state))\n  1929\t           (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n  1930\t           (update :indexer index/carry-over (:indexer state)))\n  1931\t         {:vm-type vm-type\n  1932\t          :ingress-loss? false\n  1933\t          :last-value nil\n  1934\t          :last-value-2 nil\n  1935\t          :last-value-3 nil\n  1936\t          :frontend-session nil\n  1937\t          :pending-run nil}))\n  1938\t\n  1939\t\n  1940\t(defn- configure-admission\n  1941\t  \"Apply session configuration to the linker, retaining its live state.\"\n  1942\t  [state admission]\n  1943\t  (let [linker (link/reconfigure (:linker state) admission)]\n  1944\t    (assoc state :admission admission :linker linker\n  1945\t           :link-source (:source linker))))\n   620\t(defn- sequenced-wrapper-paths\n   621\t  \"The assembled-tree path of each `sequenced` wrapper application for\n   622\t   `n` programs: the outermost wrapper at the root, each inner wrapper\n   623\t   under the previous wrapper operator's body. Assembly emits these as\n   624\t   the spec's explicit `:call-site-wrappers` occurrence set, so no\n   625\t   later step infers wrapperhood from non-coverage.\"\n   626\t  [n]\n   627\t  (vec (take (max 0 (dec n)) (iterate (fn [p] (into [2 3] p)) []))))\n   628\t\n   629\t\n   630\t(defn- recovered-call-site-claim\n   631\t  \"The C1 claim of a spec carrying `:call-site-rows` — the per-occurrence\n   632\t   rows `module-from-index` recovered and shifted into the assembled\n   633\t   tree's coordinates: those rows keep their own retained origins\n   634\t   through publication, and exactly the assembled tree applications\n   635\t   the spec's explicit `:call-site-wrappers` occurrence set names\n   636\t   (the `sequenced` wrappers assembly synthesized, as `[root path]`\n   637\t   pairs) are claimed separately under the publication admission\n   638\t   `origin`. Recovered rows and explicit wrappers together must cover\n   639\t   the tree EXACTLY: any other uncovered application — a deleted\n   640\t   retained row included — refuses the claim (`:missing`, the\n   641\t   unmapped occurrences) instead of being silently reassigned to the\n   642\t   publication origin, and a wrapper naming a covered or non-existent\n   643\t   place refuses as `:extra`. An empty or nil supplied table makes\n   644\t   no claim at all (nil), never a full claim. Same answer shapes as\n   645\t   `call-site-claim` otherwise; a recovered row of any other version\n   646\t   refuses the claim instead of publishing it.\"\n   647\t  [rows wrappers tree admission]\n   648\t  (let [origin (publication-origin admission)\n   649\t        eligible (into #{}\n   650\t                       (map (fn [[r p]] [r p]))\n   651\t                       (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n   652\t        claimed-rows (filterv (fn [row]\n   653\t                                (and (sequential? row)\n   654\t                                     (<= 4 (count row))\n   655\t                                     (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n   656\t                              (or rows []))]\n   657\t    (when (seq claimed-rows)\n   658\t      (or (when-let [[v p] (some (fn [row]\n   659\t                                   (when (not= 1 (nth row 4 nil))\n   660\t                                     [(nth row 4 nil) (nth row 2 nil)]))\n   661\t                                 claimed-rows)]\n   662\t            {:unsupported-version v, :path p})\n   663\t          (let [well-formed? (and (every? (fn [row]\n   664\t                                            (and (= 5 (count row))\n   665\t                                                 (vm/occurrence-origin? (nth row 0))\n   666\t                                                 (= (:root tree) (nth row 1))))\n   667\t                                          claimed-rows)\n   668\t                                  (= (count claimed-rows)\n   669\t                                     (count (into #{}\n   670\t                                                  (map (fn [row]\n   671\t                                                         [(nth row 1) (nth row 2)]))\n   672\t                                                  claimed-rows))))\n   673\t                covered (into #{}\n   674\t                              (map (fn [row] [(nth row 1) (nth row 2)]))\n   675\t                              claimed-rows)\n   676\t                wrapper-set (into #{}\n   677\t                                  (map (fn [[r p]] [r p]))\n   678\t                                  (or wrappers []))\n   679\t                wrappers-well? (and (every? (fn [[r p]]\n   680\t                                              (and (= (:root tree) r)\n   681\t                                                   (vector? p)))\n   682\t                                            (or wrappers []))\n   683\t                                    (= (count (or wrappers []))\n   684\t                                       (count wrapper-set)))\n   685\t                accounted (into covered wrapper-set)\n   686\t                missing (remove accounted eligible)\n   687\t                extra (concat (remove eligible covered)\n   688\t                              (remove eligible wrapper-set)\n   689\t                              (filter covered wrapper-set))]\n   690\t            (if (and well-formed? wrappers-well?\n   691\t                     (empty? missing) (empty? extra))\n   692\t              {:origin origin,\n   693\t               :rows (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\n   694\t                                (into claimed-rows\n   695\t                                      (map (fn [[r p]]\n   696\t                                             [origin r p call-site-key 1]))\n   697\t                                      wrapper-set)))}\n   698\t              {:missing (vec (sort-by pr-str missing)),\n   699\t               :extra (vec (sort-by pr-str extra))}))))))\n   700\t\n   701\t\n   702\t(defn- sequenced\n   703\t  \"One tree running `asts` in order: `((fn [_] second) first)`, nested.\n   704\t   A program root in operand position is not a tail call.  No programs\n   705\t   is `no-op-tree`.\"\n   706\t  [asts]\n   707\t  (if (empty? asts)\n   708\t    no-op-tree\n   709\t    (reduce (fn [body ast]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The exact table lookup is fixed, but recording the admission mapping still has a stale-snapshot hole: it searches all unmapped programs in the published index, not just programs committed in this round. If an older unmapped program has the same root and the new index commit or publication fails, the new admission can be attached to that older program.\n\nThe wrapper fix rejects a deleted row when the assembly’s wrapper set is unchanged. I’m checking the remaining trust boundary: whether moving that deleted occurrence into the supplied wrapper set is also rejected."}}
