{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | sed -n '570,608p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | sed -n '817,876p'; nl -ba test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | sed -n '1770,1860p'; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"   570\t   expansion's source-batch counter diverge ordinarily — a failed\n   571\t   expansion advances one, a name publication the other — so no entry\n   572\t   is ever selected by comparing them: a foreign table carrying the\n   573\t   same root and batch number under another medium or member is\n   574\t   another admission's evidence and is never borrowed. When the\n   575\t   mapping, or the entry it names, is absent, the association is\n   576\t   unavailable and recovery is refused. A matched table must still\n   577\t   prove itself: full five-coordinate rows, ruled origins, version 1,\n   578\t   unique ownership of each application, exact coverage.\"\n   579\t  [program tables admissions]\n   580\t  (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (:ast program))\n   581\t        root (:root tree)\n   582\t        eligible (into #{}\n   583\t                       (map (fn [[r p]] [r p]))\n   584\t                       (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n   585\t        origin (get admissions (:m program))\n   586\t        table (when (and (vm/occurrence-origin? origin) (map? tables))\n   587\t                (get tables [origin root]))]\n   588\t    (when (some? table)\n   589\t      (let [rows (filterv (fn [row]\n   590\t                            (and (sequential? row)\n   591\t                                 (<= 4 (count row))\n   592\t                                 (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n   593\t                          table)\n   594\t            claimed (into #{}\n   595\t                          (map (fn [row] [(nth row 1) (nth row 2)]))\n   596\t                          rows)]\n   597\t        (when (and 